    "Sorting"
  ],
  "statement": "Given a set of **distinct** positive integers `nums`, return the largest subset `answer` such that every pair `(answer[i], answer[j])` of elements in this subset satisfies:\n\n*   `answer[i] % answer[j] == 0`, or\n*   `answer[j] % answer[i] == 0`\n\nIf there are multiple solutions, return any of them.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1,2,3]\nOutput: [1,2]\nExplanation: [1,3] is also accepted.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1,2,4,8]\nOutput: [1,2,4,8]\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n*   `1 <= nums.length <= 1000`\n*   `1 <= nums[i] <= 2 * 10^(9)`\n*   All the integers in `nums` are **unique**.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= nums.length <= 1000",
    "1 <= nums[i] <= 2 * 109",
    "All the integers in nums are unique."
  ],
  "examples": [
